{"E:\\videos\\olc02\\wt\\vlog\\olc02\\voz\\b006_t2.wav": {"text": "Lars, my second cook, used to put a shake of hot sauce on top and call it a Swedish breakfast for supper. What does it cost today? About $2.60 for the whole skillet, four plates. That's 65 cents a plate. Cover first, brown after. And you know what I noticed that first night? Nobody asked where the meat was. A hot skillet of potatoes with the eggs still soft on top, a cup of coffee, and the crew went quiet. the way a crew only goes quiet when the food is good. That's when I knew we'd get through those two weeks. Supper number two, cabbage and noodles. The Polish boys in the crew called it haluski, and the first time I made it, Big Swede looked at the pot and said, that's it, cabbage? Then he had three plates, one head of green cabbage, two onions, six tablespoons of butter, or half butter and half bacon fat, 12 ounces of wide egg noodles,", "words": [{"w": " Lars,", "s": 0.02, "e": 0.56}, {"w": " my", "s": 0.56, "e": 0.66}, {"w": " second", "s": 0.66, "e": 1.06}, {"w": " cook,", "s": 1.06, "e": 1.92}, {"w": " used", "s": 1.92, "e": 2.0}, {"w": " to", "s": 2.0, "e": 2.18}, {"w": " put", "s": 2.18, "e": 2.36}, {"w": " a", "s": 2.36, "e": 2.52}, {"w": " shake", "s": 2.52, "e": 2.76}, {"w": " of", "s": 2.76, "e": 2.96}, {"w": " hot", "s": 2.96, "e": 3.2}, {"w": " sauce", "s": 3.2, "e": 3.52}, {"w": " on", "s": 3.52, "e": 3.8}, {"w": " top", "s": 3.8, "e": 4.2}, {"w": " and", "s": 4.2, "e": 4.58}, {"w": " call", "s": 4.58, "e": 4.9}, {"w": " it", "s": 4.9, "e": 5.04}, {"w": " a", "s": 5.04, "e": 5.14}, {"w": " Swedish", "s": 5.14, "e": 5.52}, {"w": " breakfast", "s": 5.52, "e": 6.0}, {"w": " for", "s": 6.0, "e": 6.32}, {"w": " supper.", "s": 6.32, "e": 7.18}, {"w": " What", "s": 7.36, "e": 7.5}, {"w": " does", "s": 7.5, "e": 7.74}, {"w": " it", "s": 7.74, "e": 7.9}, {"w": " cost", "s": 7.9, "e": 8.18}, {"w": " today?", "s": 8.18, "e": 9.04}, {"w": " About $2.60", "s": 9.08, "e": 10.68}, {"w": " for", "s": 